		"description": "Rotation as procession and spectacle. Long dual corridors lead toward a rotating centerpiece, showing how orientation and angular velocity shape spatial experience over time. Gallery, down the procession: two turntables at ten and forty degrees a second, two cubes rolling about x and about z, a plank that turns a quarter about y beside one that tips a quarter about x, rides that carry you and turn you a quarter, the other way, and a full circle, a lift that turns you half round on the way up, a scale cube, a bridge in the aisle, a ride along x that grows the space, and the diagonal.",
